      "text": "Let the day perish wherein I was born, Job 3:3. Oh that my grief were throughly weighed, Job 6:2. Why standest thou afar off, O Lord, Ps. 10:1. How long wilt thou forget me, O Lord, Ps. 13:1. why hast thou forsaken me, Ps. 22:1. Many sorrows shall be to the wicked, Ps. 32:10. Reproach hath broken my heart; and I am full of heaviness, Ps. 69:20 (69:19–21). cause my heart to despair of all the labour, Eccl. 2:20. weep day and night for the slain, Jer. 9:1. Woe is me, … that thou hast borne me a man, Jer. 15:10. I am in derision daily, Jer. 20:7.",
